1 NAME Ferdynand (Fredek) /Pamm/
2 GIVN Ferdynand (Fredek)
2 _MARNM Pamm
1 NAME פרדיננד (פרדק) /פאם/
2 GIVN פרדיננד (פרדק)
2 SURN פאם
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 28 NOV 1900
2 ADDR
3 CITY Krakow
3 STAE Lesser Poland Voivodeship
3 CTRY Poland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 6 JUN 1972
2 ADDR
3 CITY Geneva
3 STAE Geneva
3 CTRY Switzerland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Owner of a watch-fabrication plant in Geneve, Switzerland:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lusina Watch Company, Lusina Watch Factory
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Pamm	Watches; Zurich, Switzerland; registered on 14.12.1917
2 CONT
2 CONT A. Pamm Vve. & Fils	Watches; Zurich, Switzerland; registered on 06.01.1922
2 CONT
2 CONT Vve. de A. Pamm & Fils Watches; Zurich, Switzerland; registered on 04.01.1923
2 CONT
2 CONT Pamm Freres SARL	Watches; Geneva, Switzerland; registered on 5.22.1929
2 CONT
2 CONT Pamm Frères / Montres Lusina SARL	Clocks, alarm clocks, Geneva, Switzerland; registered on 8.29.1935
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lusina watch company is known to have shown ring watches at the 1939 Swiss National Exhibition. The company was known as Pamm Frères prior to 1935 and was listed as Pamm Frères, Montres Lusina, S.a.r.l , in 1966.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.mytravelwatches.com/#4 http://styleintime.com/Vintage-Watches/MANUFACTURE-L-to-Z/Lusina-Geneve
2 CONT
2 CONT Tore Pamm: André's father and his uncle, Jacub (Jaques) Pamm, were running the watch company, Lusina, until 1972 when the father of Andre and his mother died in a car crash on their way for holidays in France. As his uncle was old
2 CONC  at that time, and Andre who had worked with them for several years, had started to work in Banking some years before, they sold the company to one of their most important clients living in Iran, and I think that was the end of Lu
2 CONC sina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred Borowicz: My sister Olga is dead; she died along with her husband in a car accident in 1972. We don't know who drove the car, him or her. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.ics.uci.edu/~dan/genealogy/Krakow/Families/Grunwald.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Polish - Swiss watch manufacturer Fredek (Ferdinand) Pamm was director of the Pamm Frères watch factory in Geneva with his brother Jacob Pamm. He was born in Kraków in 1900, the son of Abraham Adolf Pamm and Regina Ryfka Frankel. 
2 CONC Pamm married Olga Horowitz-Pamm on December 7, 1926 in Wieliczka Poland. From this marriage 2 children were born, daughter Vera was the famous French biologist Professor Dr. Millou married. The son Andre initially worked in the wa
2 CONC tch business. Fredek and his wife Olga died in a tragic car accident on vacation in France on June 6, 1972. Their son Andre worked in banking after the company was sold.
2 CONT https://watch-wiki.org/index.php?title=Pamm,_Fredek
