2 CONT https://www.digitalarkivet.no/view/255/pd00000030661144
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Is Abraham his biological father?
2 CONT
2 CONT Why did Einar go by CASPARY for his last name, and not ABRAHAMSEN like his siblings and traditional Norwegian naming practices? 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1875 Norway Census, the entire household is listed as ABRAHAMSEN. In his emigration papers, he starts to use  CASPARY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Einar's mother is Nicoline NICOLAISDR and CASPARY is her surname from her father Nacolai CASPARY. At some point Einar changed his last name from ABRAHAMSEN to his mother's father's surname CASPARY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Einar's mother Nicoline Sophie NICOLAISDATTER CASPARY was the ILLEGITAMATE CHILD of Nicolai CASPARY and Karen ANDERSDATTER.  Nicoline was born on  11 Jun 1830. Karen died in June 1830.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolai CASPARY then married Anne Kirstine BORRESEN MOLLER on 07 Oct 1830.  It is believed Anne would have raised Nicoline along with three other children they had in 1832, 1834, and 1839.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicoline Sophie NICOLAISDATTER CASPARY: Birth record, Rikshospitalet, Oslo, Norway, p.199
2 CONT
2 CONT Church christening record: Rikshospitalet, Oslo, Norway, parish records (official), p. 199, #22, mother of illegitamate child, Karen ANDERSDATTER, father is said to be Nicolai CASPARY, born 11 June, 1830, christened 21 June 1830, 
2 CONC witnesses: Madame BRIEN, Ingeborg ANDERSDATTER and the goldsmith's apprentice, Christian ANDERSEN
