1 OCCU Greve
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ETABLERING AV DIPLOMATISKE FORBINDELSER MELLOM
2 CONT
2 CONT POLEN OG NORGE I ÅRENE 1919–1923
2 CONT
2 CONT pp. 295-311
2 CONT
2 CONT JAN SZYMAŃSKI
2 CONT
2 CONT University of Gdańsk
2 CONT
2 CONT The paper portrays the process of establishment and, later, development
2 CONT
2 CONT of diplomatic relations between the reborn state of Poland and Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT The issue of their regulation was discussed by the representatives of both
2 CONT
2 CONT Folia Scandinavica Posnaniensia, Vol. 9 ABSTRACTS (History)
2 CONT
2 CONT 6
2 CONT
2 CONT countries at numerous meetings during the peace treaty conference of Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a result of those negotiations, in 1919 Poland opened its mission in
2 CONT
2 CONT Christiania with Czesław Pruszyński, envoy extraordinary and minister
2 CONT
2 CONT plenipotentiary, at the helm. The mission of The Kingdom of Norway,
2 CONT
2 CONT established in 1920 in Warsaw, was headed by minister Samuel Eyde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with the resumption of diplomatic activity, both governments
2 CONT
2 CONT started work on extension of the network of consular services, which is
2 CONT
2 CONT also presented in the paper.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.staff.amu.edu.pl/~skandyn/files/Folia-vol.9-abstract-art.hist-kulturozn.pdf
