2 CONC ent some time as a house teacher at  district chief of police Rolsdorff's in Solor, appointed 7 February 1855 to personal curate  at his father's in Asker. He left this job 27 June 1857, as he had received a vocation to be  the mi
2 CONC nister of the Norwegian Church in Pointed Creek in Iowa or Wisconsin. However,  he died of typhoid fever at Asker vicarage 11 June 1857, just when he was ready to leave  for America. Unmarried.
