1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Karen Elisabeth Boe''' (Cappelen-Smith)
2 CONT
2 CONT “Bissi” Boe, formerly of Litchfield and Wilton, Conn. U.S.A., died peacefully on May 8. She was 91 years old. Bissi was born in Trondheim, Norway, the daughter of Consul Lorentz Cappelen-Smith (who spent four years in Hitler’s Gre
2 CONC ni Concentration Camp during World War II) and Lulli Bugge Cappelen-Smith, on August 5, 1917. While studying at The London School of Economics and Oxford, she was vacationing in France when World War II precluded her from returnin
2 CONC g to England or Norway. Bissi escaped the mobilization to an uncle in New York City in 1939. After completing her degree at Bryn Mawr College, she married Carsten Fritjof Boe, an engineer/inventor from Oslo, Norway in 1941. She ra
2 CONC ised a fun-loving family of six children in Delaware, Pa., Litchfield, Conn. and Castine, Maine. Carsten died in 1991. Bissi is survived by her son Carl Boe, of Scarborough, N.Y., and four daughters, Dagny Eason and Karen Miller, 
2 CONC both of Wilton, Conn., Ingri Boe-Wiegaard, of Easton, Conn., and Lulli Akin, of St. Louis, Mo., as well as 14 grandchildren and three great-grandchildren. Another son, Petter Boe, died in 1991. Bissi was buried next to her husband
2 CONC  in Litchfield, Conn. Her family and friends will miss her warm, friendly and creative personality. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Norwegian American Weeekly Vol. 120, No. 24 June 19, 2009: [https://www.norwegianamerican.com/wp-content/uploads/bsk-pdf-manager/147_DIGITAL_6-19-2009.PDF In honor and memory of Karen Elisabeth “Bissi” Boe - Aug. 5, 1917 - May 8
2 CONC , 2009]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rep. Todd Akin (R-Mo.) and wife Lulli regret to announce the death of Lulli’s mother, “Bissi” Boe. Karen Elisabeth “Bissi” Boe, formerly of Litchfield and Wilton, Conn. U.S.A., died peacefully on May 8 at the age of 91. Boe was bo
2 CONC rn in Trondheim, Norway, on Aug. 5, 1917, the daughter of Consul Lorentz Cappelen-Smith, who spent four years in Hitler’s Greni Concentration Camp during World War II, and Lulli Bugge Cappelen-Smith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Boe, who raised six children, is survived by son Carl Boe, four daughters including Lulli Akin of St. Louis, 14 grandchildren and three great-grandchildren. Another son, Petter Boe, died in 1990. Boe’s husband Carsten died in 1991
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT * Announcements, May 13, 2009 by THE HILL staff- 05/12/09: [https://thehill.com/capital-living/announcements/25114-announcements-may-13-2009 Deaths - Rep. Todd Akin (R-Mo.) and wife Lulli regret to announce the death of Lulli’s mo
2 CONC ther, Karen Elisabeth “Bissi” Boe]
