1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Augusta Guneriusdatter was born in 1872 to unmarried parents Gunerius Olsen and Hedda Amundsdatter.[1] In 1875, she was living with her maternal grandparents at Fjeld in Hedmark.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional Notes:
2 CONT She emigrated to the United States about 1897 and took the name Augusta Field.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 1900 US Census, Augusta Field was living in Chicago, Cook, Illinois, USA with her widowed aunt Thea Gundersen (born Berthea Amundsdatter)
2 CONT
