1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://gw0.geneanet.org/brynjulf?lang=no;pz=tor;nz=langballe;ocz=0;p=james;n=robertson;oc=1
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift den 20. oktober 1794, Edinburgh, Scotland, med  Katherine Deas Inglis 1775-1835 (Foreldre :  Alexander Inglis, Plantation owner in South Carolina ca 1743-1791 &   Mary Deas 1751-1785) (se notat) barn Mary Robertson 1795-1818 
2 CONC William Simon Robertson ca 1798- Alexander Inglis Robertson, Landed Proprietor 1799-1878 David Robertson ca 1800-
2 CONT  Charles Robertson, konsul for Storbritannia i Hammerfest 1801-1877 Amelia Lamont Robertson 1803 Katherine Robertson 1805/1804- Notater
2 CONT
2 CONT Notater om personen
2 CONT
2 CONT Am Baile highland history & culture The portrait of Dr James Robertson of Aultnaskiach (Altnaskiach) hangs in Inverness Town House, in the entrance hall, to the left of the staircase. The artist was John Syme, pupil and assistant 
2 CONC to Sir Henry Raeburn.
2 CONT
2 CONT A plaque reads 'In testimony of regard for his private worth; and public usefulness while Chief Magistrate of Inverness. This portrait of James Robertson of Aultnaskiack M. D. was placed here by public subscription of his fellow c
2 CONC itizens 1835'
2 CONT
2 CONT James Robertson was born in 1765, the son of Alexander Robertson, Collector of Excise.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1787 Dr Robertson was established as a medical practitioner in Inverness. He feued the lands of Aultnaskiach, which at the time was open moor land, from Davidson of Cantray. The original house faced north and the access was fro
2 CONC m Godsman's Walk. Dr Roberston closed off this once pleasant promenade much to the consternation of the people of Inverness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr Robertson was for many years a member of the Town Council. He served as Provost from 1816-18, 1824-27 and 1829-31.
2 CONT
2 CONT From early on Dr Roberston had commercial interests in the town. He was principal partner in the Wine Shop in Bridge Street and the Grocery Shop in High Street.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1825 Dr Robertson was one of the founders of 'The Northern Institution for the Promotion of Science and Literature' which existed for 10 years. He was also a Director of the Inverness Royal Academy and of the Caledonian Bank.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr Robertson retired in 1830 but he continued to give free medical advice and remained closely associated with the Northern Infirmary.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr Robertson died on 27 January 1847.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aultnaskiach House, an early-19th century mansion house in Inverness, belonged to Captain Davidson of Cantray. The lands of Cantray and Croy had been purchased by his father, Sir David Davidson, in 1767-8.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aultnaskiach House was leased by Captain Davidson to James Robertson MD, Chief Magistrate of the Burgh and Provost of Inverness on four occasions (1816-18, 1822-3, 1824-7, 1829-31). It was converted into flats in the mid-20th cent
2 CONC ury
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
